#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:118
msgid ""
"**Kaiser window** deserves special attention.  The shape parameter "
":math:`\\beta` controls the trade‑off between main‑lobe width and "
"sidelobe level.  The project includes a dedicated :math:`\\beta`-sweep "
"(``chaotic-pfc run sweep beta-sweep``) that evaluates Lyapunov exponents "
"across :math:`\\beta \\in [2, 14]` in steps of :math:`0.5` for each "
"filter type."
msgstr ""
"**Kaiser window** deserves special attention.  The shape parameter "
":math:`\\\\beta` controls the trade‑off between main‑lobe width and "
"sidelobe level.  The project includes a dedicated :math:`\\\\beta`-sweep "
"(``chaotic-pfc run sweep beta-sweep``) that evaluates Lyapunov exponents "
"across :math:`\\\\beta \\\\in [2, 14]` in steps of :math:`0.5` for each "
"filter type."

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:126
msgid "Stability and the fixed point"
msgstr "Estabilidade e o ponto fixo"

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:128
msgid ""
"When an FIR filter is inserted into the Hénon feedback loop, the Jacobian"
" matrix grows from :math:`2 \\times 2` to :math:`(2 + N_c) \\times (2 + "
"N_c)`, where :math:`N_c` is the number of filter coefficients that feed "
"back into the dynamics."
msgstr ""
"When an FIR filter is inserted into the Hénon feedback loop, the Jacobian"
" matrix grows from :math:`2 \\\\times 2` to :math:`(2 + N_c) \\\\times (2"
" + N_c)`, where :math:`N_c` is the number of filter coefficients that "
"feed back into the dynamics."

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:133
msgid ""
"The **fixed point** of the combined map‑plus‑filter system is computed by"
" solving a linear system involving the filter coefficients.  For the "
"system to have a bounded attractor, the fixed point must be finite and "
"the filter must be stable (all poles inside the unit circle)."
msgstr ""
"O **ponto fixo** do sistema combinado mapa‑mais‑filtro é calculado "
"resolvendo um sistema linear envolvendo os coeficientes do filtro.  Para "
"que o sistema tenha um atrator limitado, o ponto fixo deve ser finito e o"
" filtro deve ser estável (todos os polos dentro do círculo unitário)."

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:138
msgid ""
"The function :func:`~chaotic_pfc.dynamics.lyapunov.lyapunov_max` handles "
"the 4‑D pole‑filtered variant, which introduces an additional stability "
"parameter (pole radius :math:`r`) that must satisfy :math:`0 \\le r < 1`."
msgstr ""
"The function :func:`~chaotic_pfc.dynamics.lyapunov.lyapunov_max` handles "
"the 4‑D pole‑filtered variant, which introduces an additional stability "
"parameter (pole radius :math:`r`) that must satisfy :math:`0 \\\\le r < "
"1`."

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:143
msgid "Known limitations"
msgstr "Limitações conhecidas"

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:145
msgid ""
"**Cutoff extremes.**  :math:`\\omega_c \\to 0` produces a filter that "
"passes almost nothing (all‑stop); :math:`\\omega_c \\to 1` passes almost "
"everything (all‑pass).  Both extremes degenerate the filter and produce "
"behaviour indistinguishable from the unfiltered map — the sweep grid "
"excludes :math:`\\omega_c = 0` and :math:`\\omega_c = 1`."
msgstr ""
"**Cutoff extremes.**  :math:`\\\\omega_c \\\\to 0` produces a filter that"
" passes almost nothing (all‑stop); :math:`\\\\omega_c \\\\to 1` passes "
"almost everything (all‑pass).  Both extremes degenerate the filter and "
"produce behaviour indistinguishable from the unfiltered map — the sweep "
"grid excludes :math:`\\\\omega_c = 0` and :math:`\\\\omega_c = 1`."

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:151
msgid ""
"**Order limits.**  For :math:`N_z \\ge 40`, the filter design becomes "
"numerically ill‑conditioned (the window function has extreme values at "
"the filter edges).  The sweep currently tops at :math:`N_z = 41`."
msgstr ""
"**Order limits.**  For :math:`N_z \\\\ge 40`, the filter design becomes "
"numerically ill‑conditioned (the window function has extreme values at "
"the filter edges).  The sweep currently tops at :math:`N_z = 41`."

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:155
msgid ""
"**DC gain.**  FIR filters designed with ``firwin`` have a DC gain of "
"approximately 1.0 for lowpass , but not exactly, due to window tapering."
"  The chaotic map is sensitive to the exact coefficient magnitudes, which"
" is why the FIR bank is precomputed once rather than reconstructed per "
"grid point."
msgstr ""
"**Ganho DC.**  Filtros FIR projetados com ``firwin`` têm ganho DC de "
"aproximadamente 1,0 para passa-baixas, mas não exatamente, devido ao "
"janelamento.  O mapa caótico é sensível às magnitudes exatas dos "
"coeficientes, razão pela qual o banco FIR é pré-computado uma vez em vez "
"de reconstruído por ponto da grade."

